{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"content":"```json\n{\n  \"additions\": [\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch1:1\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0298\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供NSCLC与黑色素瘤的大样本荟萃分析数据，量化高α多样性及Akkermansia/Faecalibacterium富集对ICI生存期的正向预后效应，支撑“跨癌种共性信号”的论述。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0204\",\n          \"contribution\": \"展示HCC多界微生物组特征，揭示细菌/代谢物在持久获益与非获益组间的显著差异而真菌差异较小，用于论证微生物效应具有高度癌种特异性及多界异质性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0289\",\n          \"contribution\": \"基于SCRUM-Japan大规模队列证实整体α多样性与ICI疗效无普遍关联，且粪便口腔细菌比例升高预测较差PFS（尤其合并PPI使用时），为“无通用标志物”及统计异质性提供关键反例。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0270\",\n          \"contribution\": \"报道mCRPC患者中A. muciniphila丰度与ICI疗效呈负相关，挑战跨癌种通用正相关假设，并验证ICI治疗期间菌群高度稳定，支撑治疗方案史修饰效应及基线决定论。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch1:2\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0236\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供超5万名实体瘤患者的系统综述与荟萃分析数据，量化全身性抗生素暴露导致PFS和OS显著缩短的效应量，确立抗生素作为负面预后调节因子的流行病学证据等级。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0266\",\n          \"contribution\": \"聚焦拉丁美洲NSCLC人群，证实抗生素暴露显著降低OS但未影响PFS，提示地域/人群特征可能扰动微生物-疗效轴，补充外部干扰效应的群体异质性背景。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0289\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示质子泵抑制剂(PPI)使用者粪便中口腔细菌比例显著升高，且该特征在PPI亚组中与更差PFS趋势强相关，阐明合并用药通过重塑肠道生态位构成关键混杂/修饰变量。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0275\",\n          \"contribution\": \"针对HCC人群的Meta分析显示抗生素使用未显著恶化ICI疗效(OS/PFS/ORR)，提出肝硬化基线免疫抑制状态可能缓冲抗生素扰动，为讨论指示偏倚及肿瘤类型特异性校正必要性提供反面对照。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch1:3\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0227\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供NSCLC与黑色素瘤纵向队列数据，证明治疗初期微生物稳定性丧失独立于抗生素暴露且与ICI耐药显著相关，支持动态监测优于静态采样的核心主张。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n          \"contribution\": \"展示晚期NSCLC患者纵向多组学轨迹，发现响应者治疗后微生物特征向健康状态回归而进展期均恶化，并开发结合TMB的跨人群微生物评分，阐释动态演变与多模态分层的临床价值。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n          \"contribution\": \"针对EGFR突变NSCLC亚群，记录治疗前后微生物U型与倒U型动态演变模式及特定代谢物(脱氧胆酸、L-瓜氨酸)变化，说明驱动基因背景下的纵向生态重塑特征。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n          \"contribution\": \"报告NSCLC基线队列中肠道微生物组成、SCFA谱及肠屏障通透性指标均未能预测ICI反应或irAEs，指出标准化缺失与参考值未建立是纵向/横断面生物标志物转化的主要方法学障碍。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_key\": \"Ch1:4\",\n      \"studies\": [\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n          \"contribution\": \"报告FMT-LUMINate II期试验中NSCLC患者ORR达80%，且响应源于基线有害菌种丢失而非供体定植，提供概念验证干预的初步希望及疗效归因线索。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详述MITRIC IIa期篮子试验阴性结果(ORR 0%)，剖析快速进展疾病背景、供体匹配次优及髓系主导微环境限制等失败主因，界定FMT转化的现实边界。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐述A. muciniphila高丰度虽延长NSCLC患者OS但增加irAE风险，明确疗效与毒性在微生物层面的耦合关系，支撑安全性受ICI方案严格调节的情境依赖性论点。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n          \"contribution\": \"系统梳理早期FMT及定义菌群临床试验现状，强调多数证据来自小样本探索性研究且缺乏大型RCT确证，直接呼应Phase III空白及转化医学的证据阶梯分布特征。\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","reasoning_content":"Here's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n    - **Role/Task:** Academic review planning editor. Goal: Create a long-form review with a clear argumentative主线 (main thread). Plan substantive content in Chinese. Keep original paper titles/proper nouns. Do not write Q&A lists.\n    - **Scope Constraints:** Opening, scope declaration, abstract, and final summary are handled by independent modules *after* the main body is written. They are NOT part of this chain's chapter/unit tasks. Background, concepts, theory teaching, mechanisms, method comparisons, and future research directions needed for understanding analysis belong to the main body and should be fully expanded as needed. Each chapter must have a clear knowledge question or analytical task, not just intro/conclusion. Determine scope, perspective, and chapter division, but these planning info don't equal an entry chapter.\n    - **Chapter Organization:** Determined by research question, disciplinary context, and existing materials. No single paradigm assumed. Theory, concept, methodology, design research organized by actual argument structure. Center on user's research question. Propose overarching perspective and synthetic judgment. Different sources承担解释、比较、例证、背景或发展等职责. Don't summarize paper-by-paper. Don't let local gaps replace the main thread. Synthetic judgment must be supported by material connections/differences/evolution. Judge relevance based on RQ & materials. Correct overstatements from previous planning. Route summary vs interpretation_limits conflict -> prioritize limits. Research conditions must enter substantive_point, thesis, synthesis, transition. Don't stack conditions in a separate limitation field. Distinguish association/causation/mechanism/migration/validation/uncertainty. Limited supplementary retrieval != domain lacks research. Only describe scope supported by materials.\n    - **Current Task:** `case_groups` for `Ch1`. Pick available literature cases for already coordinated writing units. `source_materials` provides A summaries, B planning, and existing deep reads/supplements/local snippets. Read all `source_routing` & `source_materials`, compare with `unit_catalog`, pick materials that actually support the unit's objects, results, conditions, or useful contrasts. Target ~150-200 independent lit for the whole review (not per chapter/batch). Quality target, not quota. Don't repeat existing sources, don't force irrelevant ones. Only supplement specific units. New papers must add different results, conditions, methods, development stages, or useful contrasts. If only repeating same generalization, leave in pool. `additions` can be empty. Write `contribution`: ~30-60 words explaining what this material helps explain in this unit (specific writing purpose), can propose proposed synthesis. This text is specific writing purpose, NOT paper results. Methods/results/conclusions must come from attached A/B/deep reads/supplements. Recommended use cannot say analogy/scheme/other object results as direct empirical evidence for this problem. `material_available` false means no actual content, do not fabricate. Current call only responsible for one `chapter_id`. Return JSON object: `additions` array, each `unit_key`, `studies` array (`source_handle`, `contribution`).\n    - **Input Data:** I have a large JSON input containing `unit_catalog` for Ch1 with 4 units (Ch1:1 to Ch1:4), and a massive list of `source_routing` entries (P0173 to P0328) with their A/B summaries and constraints. I need to select sources for each unit that match the unit's substantive points and paragraph briefs, ensuring they provide distinct contributions (different results, conditions, methods, etc.) without repeating existing `supporting_studies` in the catalog.\n\n2.  **Deconstruct Unit Catalog (Ch1):**\n    - **Ch1:1 (U1_跨癌种关联图谱):** Substantive point: Cross-cancer observational cohorts confirm specific gut microbiome features (taxonomy/function) associated with ICI efficacy, but lack universal single marker; evidence strength varies by cancer type. Paragraph briefs: 1. Common signals vs cancer-specific distribution (Melanoma, NSCLC, RCC vs CRC, HCC reversal/failure). 2. Heterogeneity & \"no universal marker\" statistical basis (PERMANOVA, ML cross-validation poor). 3. Treatment regimen & timing modification effects (NIC vs PC arms).\n      *Existing supporting studies:* P0096, P0170, P0015.\n      *Need:* Sources that cover cross-cancer common signals, cancer-specific reversals (HCC/CRC), statistical/methodological heterogeneity (PERMANOVA/ML), and regimen/timing modification.\n    - **Ch1:2 (U2_外部干扰与宿主背景):** Substantive point: External drug exposure (antibiotics, PPIs) & combined regimens are key confounding/modifying variables, with clear time-window specificity & dose-dependence, requiring strict correction. Paragraph briefs: 1. Quantify ABT/PPI effect sizes & time windows. 2. Contrast combined regimens modifying/reversing microbial effects. 3. Emphasize correction necessity & residual bias risk (indication bias).\n      *Existing supporting studies:* P0123, P0157, P0033.\n      *Need:* Sources quantifying ABT/PPI effects/time windows, regimen modification, indication bias/correction necessity.\n    - **Ch1:3 (U3_动态监测与纵向演变):** Substantive point: Baseline single sampling misses treatment-induced ecological reshaping; longitudinal dynamic changes (pathogen clearance/colonization failure) better reflect true efficacy trajectories, but face methodological challenges. Paragraph briefs: 1. Limitations of baseline snapshots & static thresholds. 2. Predictive value of longitudinal dynamics (FMT-LUMINate data: loss of harmful species vs donor engraftment). 3. Real-world obstacles & standardization needs for longitudinal sampling.\n      *Existing supporting studies:* P0033, P0134, P0098.\n      *Need:* Sources on baseline limitations, longitudinal dynamics/FMT-LUMINate insights, sampling obstacles/standardization.\n    - **Ch1:4 (U4_证据阶梯与转化边界):** Substantive point: Evidence shows stepped distribution: strongest observational, promising but heterogeneous concept-validation interventions (FMT), Phase III RCT evidence completely missing, safety signals strictly regulated by ICI regimen. Paragraph briefs: 1. Summarize observational strength & FMT initial hope/heterogeneity. 2. Contrast negative intervention trials (MITRIC) with donor matching/disease progression speed limits. 3. Emphasize Phase III gap & context-dependent safety signals (myocarditis in dual ICI vs single PD-1).\n      *Existing supporting studies:* P0026, P0144, P0161.\n      *Need:* Sources on observational strength, FMT heterogeneity/positive trials, MITRIC/negative trials, Phase III gap, regimen-dependent safety.\n\n3.  **Map Sources to Units (Mental Filtering & Selection):**\n    I will scan the provided `source_routing` list for highly relevant papers that fit the units and haven't been used in the existing `supporting_studies`. I'll aim for 2-3 high-quality additions per unit to build a robust case base, ensuring diverse contributions.\n\n    *Unit Ch1:1 (Cross-cancer associations & heterogeneity)*\n    - Need: Cross-cancer meta-analysis, cancer-specific reversal (HCC/CRC), statistical heterogeneity/ML, regimen modification.\n    - Candidates:\n      - P0298: Meta-analysis on NSCLC & Melanoma (high alpha diversity, Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium). Good for common signals.\n      - P0204: Multi-kingdom gut microbiota in HCC (bacteria/metabolites differ between DCB/NDB, fungi less so). Good for cancer-specific/context.\n      - P0478: (Already in unit catalog cases, but I can pick another if needed. Wait, P0478 is listed in `cases` for U1. I'll skip it to avoid duplication unless necessary.)\n      - P0585: (Also in catalog cases for U1/U3).\n      - P0289: SCRUM-Japan MONSTAR-SCREEN study. Large cohort across solid tumors. Shows alpha diversity not universally predictive, oral bacteria in stool predicts worse PFS, especially with PPIs. Excellent for heterogeneity/no universal marker & external interference crossover.\n      - P0290: Meta-analysis improves identification of microbiome associations in melanoma, lung, kidney. Highlights alpha diversity inconsistent predictor, composite index better. Good for statistical/methodological point.\n      - P0270: mCRPC patients post-enzalutamide. A. muciniphila negatively associated (reversal), stable during ICI. Good for cancer-specific/regimen history modification.\n    - Selection for Ch1:1: P0298, P0204, P0289, P0270.\n    - Draft Contributions (~30-60 words each):\n      - P0298: 提供NSCLC与黑色素瘤的大样本荟萃分析数据，量化高α多样性及Akkermansia/Faecalibacterium富集对ICI生存期的正向预后效应，支撑“跨癌种共性信号”的论述。\n      - P0204: 展示HCC多界微生物组","role":"assistant"}}],"created":1791151007,"id":"chatcmpl-9d142d3e-7116-9368-92e5-215feeb6efcc","model":"qwen3.7-flash","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":3359,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2048,"text_tokens":3359},"prompt_tokens":215598,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"text_tokens":215598},"total_tokens":218957}}